chore(scope): describe the change (#ref)

# why: what problem does this solve?
# what: what changed

# BREAKING CHANGE: describe the required migration

# --------------------------------------------------
# Git commit message template.
#
# Git uses this template for a new commit message written in an editor.
# Replace the type and subject above, then add a body or footer
# if useful. Keep the subject on the first line.
#
# To use this commit template in your local repository, run:
# git config --local commit.template .gitmessage
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------
# Formatting Rules
# --------------------------

# writing style:    prefer a lowercase start and imperative wording
# type (required):  feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build,
#                   ci, chore, revert, all lowercase
# scope (optional): kebab-case, omit parentheses
#                   can describe the project, package, or tooling
# dependencies:     use deps or dev-deps as a scope
# body/footer:      seperate from the header with a blank line
# breaking change:  add ! before the colon and describe the required
#                   migration in the body/footer
# references:       replace #ref to reference an issue, PR, or commit
